<a id="Upgrading_Checkstyle_at_Runtime"></a>

# Upgrade Checkstyle at Runtime

The Maven Checkstyle Plugin has a default Checkstyle version.
For `maven-checkstyle-plugin ${project.version}`, the plugin uses Checkstyle ${checkstyleVersion} by default.

You can override the version used at runtime with a plugin dependency.
This lets you use the [latest Checkstyle checks and bug fixes](https://checkstyle.org/release-notes.html).
Declare it in `<pluginManagement>` so that it applies both to the `check` goal and to the reports:

```xml
<project>
  ...
  <build>
    <pluginManagement>
      <plugins>
        <plugin>
          <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
          <artifactId>maven-checkstyle-plugin</artifactId>
          <version>${project.version}</version>
          <dependencies>
            <dependency>
              <groupId>com.puppycrawl.tools</groupId>
              <artifactId>checkstyle</artifactId>
              <version>...choose your version...</version>
            </dependency>
          </dependencies>
        </plugin>
      </plugins>
    </pluginManagement>
  </build>
  ...
</project>
```

Newer Checkstyle versions need a newer Java version than the plugin itself.
Run Maven with a JDK that the chosen Checkstyle version supports:

| Checkstyle | Minimum Java |
|:---|:---|
| 10.x | 11 |
| 11.x and 12.x | 17 |
| 13.x and later | 21 |

The predefined `sun_checks.xml` and `google_checks.xml` rulesets come from the Checkstyle JAR.
When you upgrade Checkstyle, they change with it and can report new violations.
